{
  "level": "Uni Year 1",
  "subject": "chemistry",
  "title": "Electron configuration",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "Why subshells split",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "In hydrogen, every orbital in a shell has the same energy.", "write": "H: 2s = 2p"},
        {"say": "With more electrons, subshells split. s is lowest, then p, d and f.", "write": "ns < np < nd < nf",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 260, "alt": "Energy levels: 3s lowest, then 3p, then 4s, then 3d", "items": [
           {"kind": "arrow", "x": 60, "y": 240, "x2": 60, "y2": 20, "color": "black"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 50, "y": 30, "text": "E", "size": 20, "anchor": "end"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 120, "y": 210, "x2": 220, "y2": 210, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 240, "y": 216, "text": "3s", "size": 20, "anchor": "start"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 120, "y": 160, "x2": 220, "y2": 160, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 240, "y": 166, "text": "3p", "size": 20, "anchor": "start"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 300, "y": 110, "x2": 400, "y2": 110, "color": "orange", "change": "highlight"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 420, "y": 116, "text": "4s", "size": 20, "anchor": "start", "bold": true},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 120, "y": 80, "x2": 220, "y2": 80, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 240, "y": 86, "text": "3d", "size": 20, "anchor": "start"}
         ]}},
        {"say": "s electrons penetrate close to the nucleus, so they feel more pull.", "write": "penetration: s > p > d"},
        {"say": "That's why 4s ends up below 3d, and fills first.", "write": "4s fills before 3d"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Three rules for filling",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Aufbau: fill the lowest energy subshell first.", "write": "1s 2s 2p 3s 3p 4s 3d 4p"},
        {"say": "Use the n plus l rule. Lower n plus l fills first. On a tie, lower n wins.", "write": "4s: 4+0   3d: 3+2"},
        {"say": "Pauli: at most two electrons per orbital, with opposite spins.", "write": "max 2, ↑↓"},
        {"say": "Hund's rule is the bus-seat rule. Take an empty seat before sharing.", "write": "N: 2p ↑ ↑ ↑",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 220, "alt": "Nitrogen 2p boxes each with one up arrow", "items": [
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 130, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 230, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 330, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 280, "y": 190, "text": "N: 1s² 2s² 2p³ — 3 unpaired", "size": 20, "color": "purple"}
         ]}},
        {"say": "Oxygen's fourth p electron has to pair up in the first box.", "write": "O: 2p ↑↓ ↑ ↑",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 220, "alt": "Oxygen 2p boxes: a fourth electron pairs in the first box", "items": [
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 130, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "yellow", "label": "↑↓", "change": "add"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 230, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 330, "y": 60, "w": 100, "h": 90, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 280, "y": 190, "text": "O: 1s² 2s² 2p⁴ — 2 unpaired", "size": 20, "color": "purple"}
         ]}},
        {"say": "Unpaired electrons make an atom paramagnetic. All paired is diamagnetic.", "write": "unpaired → paramagnetic"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The two rebels: Cr and Cu",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Chromium is not 3d four, 4s two.", "write": "Cr: [Ar] 3d⁴ 4s² ✗",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 220, "alt": "Chromium: one 4s electron moves into the empty 3d box to give 3d5 4s1", "items": [
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 30, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 100, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 170, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 240, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 310, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 450, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑↓"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 205, "y": 165, "text": "3d", "size": 20},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 485, "y": 165, "text": "4s", "size": 20}
         ]}},
        {"say": "One 4s electron moves into 3d. Now d is half full.", "write": "Cr: [Ar] 3d⁵ 4s¹",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 220, "alt": "Chromium after the move: five single 3d electrons and one 4s electron", "items": [
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 30, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 100, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 170, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 240, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 310, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "yellow", "label": "↑", "change": "add"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 450, "y": 60, "w": 70, "h": 70, "fill": "white", "label": "↑"},
           {"kind": "arrow", "x": 450, "y": 45, "x2": 370, "y2": 45, "color": "red", "change": "add"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 205, "y": 165, "text": "3d", "size": 20},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 485, "y": 165, "text": "4s", "size": 20},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 280, "y": 205, "text": "half-filled d", "size": 20, "bold": true, "color": "purple"}
         ]}},
        {"say": "Copper does the same, to get a full d subshell.", "write": "Cu: [Ar] 3d¹⁰ 4s¹"},
        {"say": "4s and 3d are so close that the extra stability is worth it.", "write": "d⁵ and d¹⁰ are stable"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Configurations of ions",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Main group ions: add or remove from the highest subshell.", "write": "Cl⁻: [Ne] 3s² 3p⁶"},
        {"say": "Transition metals lose 4s electrons first. First in, first out.", "write": "Fe: [Ar] 3d⁶ 4s²",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 200, "alt": "Iron loses both 4s electrons to form Fe2+", "items": [
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 40, "y": 60, "w": 260, "h": 70, "fill": "blue", "label": "3d⁶"},
           {"kind": "rect", "x": 340, "y": 60, "w": 150, "h": 70, "fill": "orange", "label": "4s²", "change": "remove"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 280, "y": 175, "text": "Fe²⁺ = [Ar] 3d⁶", "size": 24, "bold": true, "color": "purple", "change": "add"}
         ]}},
        {"say": "So iron two plus is argon 3d six. Iron three plus is 3d five.", "write": "Fe³⁺: [Ar] 3d⁵"},
        {"say": "Always write the neutral atom first, then take electrons away.", "write": "atom first, then ion"},
        {"say": "Same configuration means isoelectronic, like O two minus, F minus and neon.", "write": "O²⁻, F⁻, Ne, Na⁺"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Effective nuclear charge",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Inner electrons shield outer ones from the nucleus.", "write": "Z_eff = Z − S",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 280, "alt": "Nucleus with core electrons shielding a valence electron", "items": [
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 200, "y": 140, "r": 110, "fill": "none"},
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 200, "y": 140, "r": 60, "fill": "grey", "label": "core e⁻"},
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 200, "y": 140, "r": 22, "fill": "red", "label": "+Z"},
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 310, "y": 140, "r": 16, "fill": "yellow", "label": "e⁻", "change": "highlight"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 440, "y": 120, "text": "feels Z − S", "size": 22, "bold": true, "color": "purple"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 440, "y": 155, "text": "not the full Z", "size": 18}
         ]}},
        {"say": "Slater's rules: same group electrons count 0.35 each.", "write": "same group: 0.35"},
        {"say": "Shell n minus one counts 0.85. Deeper shells count 1.00.", "write": "n−1: 0.85   lower: 1.00"},
        {"say": "Across a period, Z rises but shielding barely does. So Z eff rises.", "write": "across: Z_eff ↑"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Periodic trends",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Higher Z eff pulls electrons in. Radius shrinks across a period.", "write": "across: radius ↓"},
        {"say": "Ionisation energy and electronegativity go up across a period.", "write": "across: IE ↑, EN ↑"},
        {"say": "Down a group, n increases, so atoms get bigger.", "write": "down: radius ↑, IE ↓"},
        {"say": "Two dips. Be beats B, and N beats O.", "write": "Be > B,  N > O",
         "draw": {"type": "shapes", "width": 560, "height": 260, "alt": "First ionisation energy across period 2 with dips at boron and oxygen", "items": [
           {"kind": "line", "x": 40, "y": 220, "x2": 530, "y2": 220, "color": "black"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 70, "y": 190, "x2": 130, "y2": 150, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 130, "y": 150, "x2": 190, "y2": 170, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 190, "y": 170, "x2": 250, "y2": 120, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 250, "y": 120, "x2": 310, "y2": 80, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 310, "y": 80, "x2": 370, "y2": 95, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 370, "y": 95, "x2": 430, "y2": 50, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "line", "x": 430, "y": 50, "x2": 490, "y2": 20, "color": "blue"},
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 190, "y": 170, "r": 9, "fill": "red", "change": "highlight"},
           {"kind": "circle", "x": 370, "y": 95, "r": 9, "fill": "red", "change": "highlight"},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 70, "y": 245, "text": "Li", "size": 16},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 130, "y": 245, "text": "Be", "size": 16},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 190, "y": 245, "text": "B", "size": 16, "bold": true},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 250, "y": 245, "text": "C", "size": 16},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 310, "y": 245, "text": "N", "size": 16},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 370, "y": 245, "text": "O", "size": 16, "bold": true},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 430, "y": 245, "text": "F", "size": 16},
           {"kind": "text", "x": 490, "y": 245, "text": "Ne", "size": 16}
         ]}},
        {"say": "Boron's electron is in higher-energy 2p. Oxygen's fourth p electron feels pairing repulsion.", "write": "B: 2p   O: pairing"},
        {"say": "A big jump in successive ionisation energies shows you've hit a core shell.", "write": "big jump = core shell"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Watch out for these",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Don't remove 3d before 4s. Iron two plus is not 3d four 4s two.", "write": "✗ Fe²⁺: [Ar] 3d⁴ 4s²"},
        {"say": "Don't pair electrons too early. Fill each box singly first.", "write": "✗ ↑↓ before ↑ ↑ ↑"},
        {"say": "Don't just say more protons. Explain Z eff, shielding and distance.", "write": "Z_eff + shielding + distance"},
        {"say": "Copper one plus is 3d ten. Copper two plus is 3d nine.", "write": "Cu⁺ 3d¹⁰   Cu²⁺ 3d⁹"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {"say": "Aufbau, Pauli and Hund build every configuration.", "write": "Aufbau, Pauli, Hund"},
        {"say": "4s: first in, first out.", "write": "4s first in, first out"},
        {"say": "Chromium and copper cheat for a happier d.", "write": "Cr 3d⁵ 4s¹  Cu 3d¹⁰ 4s¹"},
        {"say": "Z eff rises across a period: smaller atoms, higher ionisation energy.", "write": "Z_eff ↑ → radius ↓"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
